From a68b375172b0da71d2c4a61c6585f4512468b7fa Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 11:48:57 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 07/15] Round 7: Encode typed metrics once as raw JSON

Build complete, stop and unfinished metrics from typed structs whose
fields follow the sorted key order of the former Value maps, encode
them once into a Box<RawValue> and splice that into records. Interval
fields are declared in the same sorted order. A test checks that every
metrics shape re-serializes byte for byte through a sorted Value, and
the CLI output for complete, work-limited and infeasible requests is
unchanged.

Workload: serial with full records (96 candidates, one worker), 11 samples.
Before median: 0.117 ms. After median: 0.093 ms. Speedup: 1.26x.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
